{
  "result": "If I had one wish to change the world, I would make radical empathy our default setting.\n\nNot just being *nice* to each other, but truly being able to feel and understand each other's lives for a moment - what it's like to be in someone else's shoes, their fears, their hopes, their history.\n\nI think if we had that, so many other problems would start to fix themselves.\n\nWars are harder to start when you deeply feel the cost to the other side. Poverty and hunger are harder to ignore when you feel how heavy they are to live through. Loneliness, division, cruelty online - they all get softer when people really *see* each other.\n\nI wouldn't want to erase our differences - our different cultures, opinions, and weird little quirks are what make the world interesting. But if understanding came before judgment, we'd still disagree, we'd just do it with curiosity instead of hate.\n\nIt's a quiet superpower, but I think it's the one that would unlock all the others.\n\nWhat about you? If you had that one wish - what would you change?",
